# The work-area overlay: Work areas tints every node a gatherer's worker searches. A stonecutter's site stands near the stone
# heaps at 26,17 and 24,15. The digest stays the same with the overlay on and off, and a new seed turns it off.
# Run it on the game view with seed 1234567812345678 and size 1:
#   sh tools/play-run.sh work-areas --game-view --seed 1234567812345678 --size 1 --fps 10
# The castle's click places it at 24,19. The stonecutter's site goes to 28,18.
click-tile 24 19
wait 0.3
expect-at 24 19 building
button Stonecutter
click-tile 28 18
button Stonecutter
wait 0.3
expect-at 28 18 building

# The ticks hold from the fast-forward until the next shot, so the digest before and after the press is of one tick.
fast-forward until ticks >= 40 max 100
expect digest = da62d96f83fc3cae
button Work areas
wait 0.3
expect digest = da62d96f83fc3cae
shot tint 28 18 7 1

# Off again: the tint is gone.
button Work areas
wait 0.3
shot untinted 28 18 7 1

# A new seed starts a new game, and Work areas starts off: the new map shows no tint.
button Work areas
wait 0.3
seed 1234567812345634
wait 0.3
expect seed = 1234567812345634
shot new-seed
